    <briefdescription>
<para>Represents a range of memset&apos;d bytes with the ByteVal value. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This allows us to analyze stores like: store 0 -&gt; P+1 store 0 -&gt; P+0 store 0 -&gt; P+3 store 0 -&gt; P+2 which sometimes happens with stores to arrays of structs etc. When we see the first store, we make a range [1, 2). The second store extends the range to [0, 2). The third makes a new range [2, 3). The fourth store joins the two ranges into [0, 3) which is memset&apos;able. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
